NAME
       load_policy - load the SELinux policy into the kernel

SYNOPSIS
       load_policy

DESCRIPTION
       load_policy reads the policy of the type named in /etc/selinux/config
       (targeted on RHEL) and loads it into the kernel. The boot process
       does this normally, so you rarely run it. Tools such as semodule and
       setsebool -P reload the policy themselves.

       You may meet it in an emergency shell (for example after rd.break and
       chroot /sysroot), where no policy is loaded yet; load_policy -i loads
       it there so labels can be set right.

EXAMPLES
           load_policy

SEE ALSO
       selinux(8), semodule(8), fixfiles(8)
